<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dragoș, Voivode of Moldavia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1350</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dragoș was a Romanian noble from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maramures">Maramureș</a> who, according to tradition, was sent by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-of-hungary">Louis I of Hungary</a> around 1346–1347 to found a frontier march on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moldova">Moldova</a> river against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>. Remembered as the first voivode of Moldavia, he was followed by his son and grandson until Bogdan I expelled them around 1359. Legend tells that he crossed the mountains while hunting an aurochs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dragos-voivode-of-moldavia.jpg" alt="Dragoș, Voivode of Moldavia" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Post of Moldova · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stamp_of_Moldova_189.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
